{
  "id": "COMPOUND:38271 - PROTEIN:5854",
  "verbalization": "Sasanquasaponin I appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to a relationship with LNCaP, a prostate cancer cell line. The evidence suggests that Sasanquasaponin I may act through the SDR family member 9, which is targeted by N-Methyltyramine, or through Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is targeted by (+)-Menthol. Both of these targets are implicated in cellular processes that could influence LNCaP cell behavior. The shared involvement of Microtubule-associated protein 1B across different pathways indicates a potential role in cell proliferation or survival, which could be relevant to LNCaP. The presence of multiple targets and their downstream effects on LNCaP suggests a possible mechanism involving cellular signaling pathways that are dysregulated in prostate cancer. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Sasanquasaponin I and LNCaP, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
